-- =========================================================================
-- AI — the 2 `AI` PROVIDER instances, authored as Fenel typed values
-- (module-substrate Phase 3l: providers ARE values; carbon-copy of email's
-- `instances.fenel`).
--
-- An instance is a typed VALUE of the capability type: `aiAnthropic : AI
-- anthropic` is a value whose type is `AI` applied to the provider tag
-- `anthropic`. `loadFenelModule(..., {dispatchInstanceFile:true})` projects
-- each into the `ClassInstance { typeName:"AI", args:[<provider>], methods,
-- label, priority }` shape the registry's `listProvidersSorted` +
-- `resolveCapabilityMethod` read — exactly the codec / email pattern.
--
-- The `complete` method is an fnId STRING — the qualified dispatch name
-- `AI.<provider>.complete` (codec's instances no longer do this: they write
-- the reference `encode = codec.base64Encode`). `resolveCapabilityMethod`
-- returns this string as its `spec`;
-- the runtime dispatch keys off `provider.args[0]` + the method name (NOT the
-- spec), so the string is the browsable/identifying value, never executed
-- directly. The 3k loader fix drops `priority` from the projected methods
-- record (it is lifted to the instance `priority` slot).
--
-- PRIORITY ORDER (preserved byte-identical from the retired const): anthropic
-- 10 < openai 20. `listProvidersSorted` ranks HIGHER priority first, so
-- `openai` ranks first and `resolveCapabilityMethod("AI.complete")` resolves
-- to `openai`. Do NOT "fix" to anthropic-first. `label` is the dev-facing
-- provider name.
-- =========================================================================

aiAnthropic : AI "anthropic"
aiAnthropic = AI { complete = "AI.anthropic.complete", label = "Anthropic (Claude)", priority = 10 }

aiOpenai : AI "openai"
aiOpenai = AI { complete = "AI.openai.complete", label = "OpenAI (GPT)", priority = 20 }
